---
/**
 * Spotlight section for the Word Study feature — the app's clearest
 * differentiator from competitors. Two-column layout: the pitch on the
 * left, a stylised "lookup card" preview on the right that mirrors what
 * the user actually sees in the app.
 */
---

<section id="word-study" class="border-t border-divider">
  <div
    class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 md:py-28 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 md:gap-16 items-center"
  >
    <!-- Pitch column -->
    <div>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-accent">
        Word study
      </p>
      <h2
        class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink leading-tight"
      >
        Original meaning, instantly.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
        Every word in the King James Bible maps to its underlying Hebrew or
        Greek root. Hold any word — see the lemma, transliteration, part of
        speech, and a one-paragraph definition. The full Strong's
        Concordance, all offline.
      </p>

      <dl class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-4 max-w-md">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-accent">5,624</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft">Greek lemmas</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-accent">8,674</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft">Hebrew lemmas</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-accent">9,800+</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft">English surface forms</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-accent">0</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft">Network calls required</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <!-- Mocked lookup card — visual echo of the in-app UI without
         loading the actual app. Stays in cream-on-cream for cohesion. -->
    <div class="relative md:justify-self-end w-full max-w-md">
      <div
        class="rounded-2xl bg-cream-2 ring-1 ring-divider p-6 shadow-[0_20px_60px_-20px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)]"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span
            class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-accent bg-accent/10 px-2 py-1 rounded"
          >
            Word Study
          </span>
          <span class="text-xs italic text-ink-muted">"agape"</span>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-cream p-5 ring-1 ring-divider/60">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span
              class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-wider uppercase text-cream bg-[#3563B5]/85 px-2 py-1 rounded"
            >
              Greek · G26
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-ink-muted">noun, fem.</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 font-serif text-3xl text-ink">ἀγάπη</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm italic text-accent">agápē</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            Love — chiefly self-giving, choice-driven love. The love that
            defines God's nature in 1 John 4:8.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink-muted text-center">
          Hold any word in the reader → see the original.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
